# PLOS Computational Biology — LaTeX rules

Canonical manuscript: [`docs/paper/plos_my_paper.tex`](docs/paper/plos_my_paper.tex). Read-only template reference: [`docs/paper/plos_template.tex`](docs/paper/plos_template.tex).

Official guides: [LaTeX](https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/s/latex), [Submission guidelines](https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/s/submission-guidelines), [Figures](https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/s/figures).

## Structure (single file)

- One `.tex` file only — **no** `\input`, `\externaldocument`, or `\include` for manuscript body.
- Do **not** delete packages listed in the PLOS template preamble.
- Section order: Title page → Abstract → Author summary → Introduction → Results → Discussion → Materials and methods → Acknowledgments → References → Supporting information captions.
- Use `\section*{}` for unnumbered main sections; **≤3** heading levels (`\section*`, `\subsection*`, `\subsubsection*`).
- `\linenumbers` after `\newgeometry`; remove before final acceptance.

## Figures and tables

- **No `\includegraphics`** in the manuscript `.tex` — figures upload separately at submission.
- Use caption-only `\begin{figure}...\end{figure}`; describe panels in the caption (**A:**, **B:**, …), not `\subfigure`.
- Cite **Fig** (not Figure), **Table**, **Eq** (not Equation).
- Place each figure/table environment **immediately after** the first paragraph that cites it (read order).
- Submission file names: `Fig1.tif`, `Fig2.tif`, … (match `\label{fig1}` citations).
- Combined multi-panel figures = one image file before upload.

## Text and style

- Title: sentence case, ≤200 characters. Short title ≤70 characters.
- Abstract: ≤300 words, **no citations**.
- Author summary: 150–200 words, **first person** (required for PLOS Comp Biol).
- Species: italics, e.g. `\textit{Mus musculus}`.
- No footnotes. No colored `\todo{}` in submission PDF — use `% TODO:` comments only.
- No graphics or colored text in body (table cell shading via `xcolor` OK).

## References and availability

- `\bibliographystyle{plos2025}` + `\bibliography{references}`; bib file: [`docs/paper/references.bib`](docs/paper/references.bib).
- Vancouver numbered citations via `\cite{}`.
- Include **Data availability** and **Code availability** statements in Materials and methods.
- Funding/competing interests go in Editorial Manager fields, not Acknowledgments body.

## Supporting information

- List SI captions at end of manuscript (`\paragraph*{S1 Fig.}` + `\label{S1_Fig}`).
- Cite SI with `\nameref{S1_Fig}` when needed.

## Agent workflow

- Edit `plos_my_paper.tex`, not `plos_template.tex`.
- Export figures via `scripts/paper/` → `docs/paper/figures/` and copy to Overleaf upload folder.
- [`paper/overleaf/`](paper/overleaf/) is figure/table staging only.
